sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch05-26--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch05-26: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.44";
    dc:description "Electron microscopy of Paramecium, Tetrahymena and some crustacean sperm can test whether odd outlines are braced by fibrils. The mechanical claim, that those fibrils are elastic restraints equivalent to Plateau's wires, needs perturbation or stiffness data that are not archived for the stated groups. Existing images therefore cover a structural proxy for a few species.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Map intracellular fibrils onto the spiral or other non-equilibrium outline of decapod sperm and ciliates, and ask whether the outline relaxes when those fibrils are absent. A fibrillar scaffold whose geometry matches the departure from a surface-tension figure would support the claim; the same outlines without such fibrils, or fibrils that do not follow the spiral, would weaken it.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Cortex and sperm ultrastructure are spread across individual papers, with quantitative shape-versus-fibril tables for only a few model ciliates.", "Nearly all of these cells have a cytoskeleton, so presence alone does not show that the fibrils act as Plateau frames.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.5"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.443"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch05-26--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of thompson1917-ch05-26 by Grok 4.7: 0.4";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.4"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch05-26--grok>.
